Element Tree ⭐

This is an important Happiest Minds interview topic, and you actually asked about it before.

You previously wondered:

“Everything we see in Flutter is a widget, so what is an Element?”

Simple explanation

A Widget is a configuration/description of what the UI should be.

An Element is the persistent connection between a Widget and its position in the Widget Tree.

Think:

Widget
   ↓
Element
   ↓
RenderObject

But don't treat them as the same thing.

Why do we need Elements?

Widgets are immutable and can be recreated frequently.

Flutter needs something that can persist between rebuilds and keep track of the widget's place in the tree.

That's where the Element Tree comes in.

For example:

Widget Tree          Element Tree
-----------          ------------
Scaffold       →     Scaffold Element
   ↓                     ↓
 Text          →     Text Element

When Flutter rebuilds, it can compare the new widgets with existing elements and decide whether an existing element can be reused.

That's why you previously heard:

“The Element Tree decides whether to reuse existing elements.”

That's the concept.


